Modifications made for vendoring (recorded in the project git history via
the .dejavue/timeline.jsonl log and the round-12 PR body):

1. Diverged from the round-11 `List` vendoring pattern: round-12 ships as
   `Widget` only (not `Widget` AND `StatefulWidget`) because upstream
   ratatui's BarChart has no `StatefulWidget` counterpart. The §3
   module doc in this crate explicitly notes that the round-11 E0034
   carve-out pattern does NOT apply here (BarChart is round-6 Tabs
   pattern stateless), so a future stateful-widget-vendoring round
   does not inherit the contract for the wrong shape.

2. The vendored `BarChart`'s `direction` field uses
   `ratatui::layout::Direction` directly via `pub use ratatui::layout::Direction;`
   — different from round-11's vendored `Direction` enum (which was a
   custom `TopToBottom`/`BottomToTop`). The choice matches upstream
   ratatui 1:1.

3. The vendored `BarChart::render` paints per-bar `Style` patches via
   per-cell `cell.set_style(...)` after the underlying `set_line` call
   — defends against the ratatui 0.30 `set_line` per-Span-style
   propagation inconsistency that round-11's vendored `List` had to
   work around in v18.

4. Six inline smoke tests + six integration tests (matches round-11's
   count for parity). Two differentiator tests close specific hazard
   categories: `bar_chart_direction_arms_yield_distinct_cell_anchors`
   (closes Direction arm silent no-op) and
   `bar_chart_max_scales_tallest_bar_to_full_height` (closes max-value
   scaling confusion with column-width scaling).

